From bee382099af0d3733432f7aebe48185a98f53aed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: briansp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:43:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] moe-cache: in-place prefill expert reads for a pinned host
 master (no whole-table staging above the band)

With host experts (-ncmoe) and the MoE expert cache, every prefill ubatch above the band copied each routed
expert table whole: from the host into the scheduler ring slot, then (-sm tensor) stage_d2d into the tensor.
The cache's arena already holds the hot experts on the device, and a pinned host master is GPU-readable.

- Cache-aware staging (moe_cache_stage_table): when a whole-table staging copy is exactly a registered table's
  slice, fill it with one kernel instead - resident experts from the arena, the rest from the pinned host alias.
- In-place reads: the staging is deferred instead.  stage_d2d hands the record from the ring slot to the tensor
  and skips the copy, and the tensor's consumer either reads the table in place (the routed-compact MMQ kernel
  takes an arena / slot map / host alias source per expert) or fills it first (any other consumer, the fused gate
  stream), so every other path still sees the original bytes.  The geometry is read live at the consumer.
- Tail guard: MMQ reads one K tile past an expert's last row.  For the table's last expert read from the host that
  runs off the end of the host table, so a routed, non-resident last expert is copied to a zero-padded scratch.
- Below the staging width gate (17-63 tokens) a split still stages when every host weight in it is served in place
  (staging copies nothing), via a new moe_cache_inplace backend hook (CUDA per device, meta = all devices).
- offload_op sends a routed op to the GPU above the band when its table is served in place: 17-31-token routed
  batches were running on the CPU (the 32-token offload minimum).

Pinned host master only (cudaHostGetDevicePointer succeeded); otherwise everything stays as before.
GGML_MOE_CACHE_INPLACE=0 keeps the cache-aware staging copy, GGML_MOE_CACHE_STAGE=0 restores the plain upload.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
